                                    <h2><span class="shaft"><img src="//cdn.recordinghacks.com/images/icons/patterns/icon_9.png" id="1189-0" width=27 height=27 alt="9 polar patterns" title="Cardioid, Omni, Figure 8, and six intermediate positions" ></span>Blackspade Acoustics UM17R</h2>
                    
                    <h2 class="sub">                    Multi-Pattern Tube Condenser Microphone</h2>
                    <p>The UM17R is a multipattern tube condenser microphone made in the US by AMI. It is the premium edition of the company&#8217;s UM17, and differs from the UM17 in the following ways:</p><ul><li>The Blackspade K17 capsule in the UM17 is swapped for a Thiersch M7, a Mylar-diaphragmmed M7 capsule made in Germany.</li><li>The Chinese shockmount is swapped for a custom-made Rycote shockmount.</li><li>The imported power supply from the UM17 is swapped for a supply designed and manufactured in the US by AMI. The UM17R will likely have a 9-pattern switch (rather than 11, as on the UM17).</li><li>The cable is upgraded to Gotham GAC-7, with Switchcraft connectors.</li></ul><p>Like the UM17, the UM17R employs an amplifier circuit and transformer designed by AMI.</p><p>The transformer is a BV8LP, a smaller version of the BV8 transformer used in the Neumann U47.</p><p>The tube is a NOS EF732/5840, made by either Telefunken or Sylvania.</p><p>The UM17R ships with a Rycote shockmount, a power supply, Gotham cable, and a flight case. It is covered by a 5-year warranty.<p>Permalink: <a href="//recordinghacks.com/microphones/Blackspade/UM17R">Blackspade Acoustics UM17R</a></p><p>The mic was released in 2011.</p>
